{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":76318,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"9a736159-0f0d-5337-990b-841766e9db5b","total_cost_usd":0.560034,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9065,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":7500,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9065,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7500,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9065},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3629,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.003714,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":7500,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":9065,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.55632,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-h1-reviewer-fable-36\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:46f08f48dfee5b1142a4\",\"verdict\":\"demonstrated_issue\",\"issue_class\":\"issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure\",\"bounded_statement\":\"Within case:46f08f48dfee5b1142a4 only: the exact two-sided binomial test in workflow/analysis.py treats all 24 bout rows as independent trials (18 UV picks of 24, reported p = 0.0227, null rejected), even though data-description.md designates colony_id as the independent-unit column and states that the three rows per colony are related rather than free-standing. Each of the 8 colonies therefore enters the row-independent binomial procedure three times. Collapsing to one outcome per independent unit (6 of 8 colonies UV-majority) gives an exact two-sided binomial p ≈ 0.289, so the report's stated rejection of the null at alpha = 0.05 is not supported by an analysis at the authorized independent unit.\",\"root_cause\":\"analysis.py computes a per-row UV pick for every bout and passes n_uv and n_bouts (24) directly into scipy.stats.binomtest, so each colony's three correlated bouts are counted as three independent Bernoulli trials; the workflow never aggregates to the colony level or otherwise models within-colony dependence, inflating the effective sample size from 8 independent units to 24 rows and producing the anticonservative p = 0.0227.\",\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The data description names colony_id as the independent-unit column and explicitly states that rows sharing a colony_id are related, not free-standing observations.\",\"observed_value\":\"independent unit = colony_id; 3 related rows per colony\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":10,\"end_line\":12,\"quoted_text\":\"One row is: one foraging bout by one colony, with the landing tallies for both arrays\\nIndependent unit column: colony_id\\nOne trial is: one row\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":22,\"end_line\":24,\"quoted_text\":\"The three bouts belonging to a colony draw on the same set of foragers and the\\nsame colony-level state, so rows sharing a colony_id are related to one another\\nrather than free-standing observations.\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":15,\"end_line\":15,\"quoted_text\":\"- colony_id: label of the source colony, C01 through C08; three rows carry each label\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow scores one pick per row and feeds all 24 row-level outcomes into a single binomial test, so each colony enters the row-independent procedure three times.\",\"observed_value\":\"binomtest(n_uv=18, n_bouts=24, p0=0.5)\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":30,\"end_line\":33,\"quoted_text\":\"    bouts = load_bouts(DATA)\\n    picks = [picked_uv(row) for row in bouts]\\n    n_bouts = len(picks)\\n    n_uv = sum(picks)\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":41,\"end_line\":41,\"quoted_text\":\"    test = binomtest(n_uv, n_bouts, NULL_PREFERENCE, alternative=\\\"two-sided\\\")\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report asserts that each bout is an independent trial and rejects the null at alpha = 0.05 on that basis (p = 0.0227).\",\"observed_value\":\"p = 0.0227 with n = 24 bout-level trials; null rejected\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":24,\"end_line\":26,\"quoted_text\":\"Exact two-sided binomial test on the 24 bout outcomes against a null\\nUV-pick probability of 0.500; each bout enters the test as one\\nindependent trial.\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":30,\"end_line\":30,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Exact binomial test: 18 UV picks in 24 bouts (observed share 0.750), two-sided p = 0.0227 against p0 = 0.500; foragers picked the UV-reflective array more often than the null preference.\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":32,\"end_line\":32,\"quoted_text\":\"Null hypothesis rejected at alpha = 0.05: yes.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The input data confirm three rows per colony_id (e.g., C01 appears on three consecutive rows), so every independent unit contributes three entries to the test.\",\"observed_value\":\"8 colonies x 3 bouts = 24 rows\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":2,\"end_line\":4,\"quoted_text\":\"C01,1,left,41,17,20\\nC01,2,right,38,22,22\\nC01,3,left,44,15,18\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report's own per-colony table shows strong within-colony clustering of picks (five colonies at 3/3 UV, one at 0/3), inconsistent with the independent-trials assumption and material to the result: at the colony level only 6 of 8 colonies are UV-majority, giving exact two-sided binomial p ≈ 0.289 (2 x 37/256), which does not reject the null at alpha = 0.05.\",\"observed_value\":\"colony-level: 6/8 UV-majority colonies, p ≈ 0.2891 vs reported row-level p = 0.0227\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":13,\"end_line\":20,\"quoted_text\":\"| C01 | 3 | 3 |\\n| C02 | 3 | 3 |\\n| C03 | 3 | 3 |\\n| C04 | 3 | 3 |\\n| C05 | 3 | 3 |\\n| C06 | 2 | 3 |\\n| C07 | 1 | 3 |\\n| C08 | 0 | 3 |\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The data description itself states 'One trial is: one row', and the workflow follows that trial definition exactly; this could be read as authorizing the per-bout test. However, the same document designates colony_id as the independent-unit column and declares rows sharing a colony_id to be related, and a trial definition does not confer the independence the binomial procedure requires, so this does not overturn the finding.\",\"observed_value\":\"trial defined as one row, but independence explicitly denied for rows sharing colony_id\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":12,\"end_line\":12,\"quoted_text\":\"One trial is: one row\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report is transparent about its assumption and discloses the full per-colony breakdown, so nothing is hidden; but disclosure does not repair the test, and the disclosed breakdown itself evidences the within-colony dependence that invalidates the 24-trial assumption.\",\"observed_value\":\"assumption disclosed; per-colony table provided\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":11,\"end_line\":12,\"quoted_text\":\"| colony | UV picks | bouts |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":25,\"end_line\":26,\"quoted_text\":\"UV-pick probability of 0.500; each bout enters the test as one\\nindependent trial.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I tried to show the row-level test is harmless by re-running the analysis at the authorized independent unit. First I verified the reported statistic is internally correct: with 18 successes in 24 trials at p0 = 0.5, the exact two-sided p is 2 x 190051/2^24 ≈ 0.0227, matching the report, so the discrepancy is not a computation error. Then I aggregated to one outcome per colony: colonies C01-C06 are UV-majority (C06 at 2/3) while C07 and C08 are white-majority, giving 6 of 8 UV-majority colonies and an exact two-sided binomial p = 2 x (28+8+1)/256 ≈ 0.289 > 0.05; pooling raw visit counts within colony gives the same 6-of-8 split. I also checked whether the picks could plausibly be independent despite the shared colony label: the per-colony distribution (five colonies at 3/3, one at 0/3) is strongly overdispersed relative to independent Bernoulli(0.75) trials, confirming within-colony correlation. Every attempt to rescue the reported rejection at the colony level failed, so I could not falsify the issue.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-h1-reviewer-fable-36","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:46f08f48dfee5b1142a4","verdict":"demonstrated_issue","issue_class":"issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure","bounded_statement":"Within case:46f08f48dfee5b1142a4 only: the exact two-sided binomial test in workflow/analysis.py treats all 24 bout rows as independent trials (18 UV picks of 24, reported p = 0.0227, null rejected), even though data-description.md designates colony_id as the independent-unit column and states that the three rows per colony are related rather than free-standing. Each of the 8 colonies therefore enters the row-independent binomial procedure three times. Collapsing to one outcome per independent unit (6 of 8 colonies UV-majority) gives an exact two-sided binomial p ≈ 0.289, so the report's stated rejection of the null at alpha = 0.05 is not supported by an analysis at the authorized independent unit.","root_cause":"analysis.py computes a per-row UV pick for every bout and passes n_uv and n_bouts (24) directly into scipy.stats.binomtest, so each colony's three correlated bouts are counted as three independent Bernoulli trials; the workflow never aggregates to the colony level or otherwise models within-colony dependence, inflating the effective sample size from 8 independent units to 24 rows and producing the anticonservative p = 0.0227.","evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description names colony_id as the independent-unit column and explicitly states that rows sharing a colony_id are related, not free-standing observations.","observed_value":"independent unit = colony_id; 3 related rows per colony","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":10,"end_line":12,"quoted_text":"One row is: one foraging bout by one colony, with the landing tallies for both arrays\nIndependent unit column: colony_id\nOne trial is: one row"},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":22,"end_line":24,"quoted_text":"The three bouts belonging to a colony draw on the same set of foragers and the\nsame colony-level state, so rows sharing a colony_id are related to one another\nrather than free-standing observations."},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":15,"end_line":15,"quoted_text":"- colony_id: label of the source colony, C01 through C08; three rows carry each label"}]},{"description":"The workflow scores one pick per row and feeds all 24 row-level outcomes into a single binomial test, so each colony enters the row-independent procedure three times.","observed_value":"binomtest(n_uv=18, n_bouts=24, p0=0.5)","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":30,"end_line":33,"quoted_text":"    bouts = load_bouts(DATA)\n    picks = [picked_uv(row) for row in bouts]\n    n_bouts = len(picks)\n    n_uv = sum(picks)"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":41,"end_line":41,"quoted_text":"    test = binomtest(n_uv, n_bouts, NULL_PREFERENCE, alternative=\"two-sided\")"}]},{"description":"The report asserts that each bout is an independent trial and rejects the null at alpha = 0.05 on that basis (p = 0.0227).","observed_value":"p = 0.0227 with n = 24 bout-level trials; null rejected","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":24,"end_line":26,"quoted_text":"Exact two-sided binomial test on the 24 bout outcomes against a null\nUV-pick probability of 0.500; each bout enters the test as one\nindependent trial."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":30,"end_line":30,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Exact binomial test: 18 UV picks in 24 bouts (observed share 0.750), two-sided p = 0.0227 against p0 = 0.500; foragers picked the UV-reflective array more often than the null preference."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":32,"end_line":32,"quoted_text":"Null hypothesis rejected at alpha = 0.05: yes."}]},{"description":"The input data confirm three rows per colony_id (e.g., C01 appears on three consecutive rows), so every independent unit contributes three entries to the test.","observed_value":"8 colonies x 3 bouts = 24 rows","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":4,"quoted_text":"C01,1,left,41,17,20\nC01,2,right,38,22,22\nC01,3,left,44,15,18"}]},{"description":"The report's own per-colony table shows strong within-colony clustering of picks (five colonies at 3/3 UV, one at 0/3), inconsistent with the independent-trials assumption and material to the result: at the colony level only 6 of 8 colonies are UV-majority, giving exact two-sided binomial p ≈ 0.289 (2 x 37/256), which does not reject the null at alpha = 0.05.","observed_value":"colony-level: 6/8 UV-majority colonies, p ≈ 0.2891 vs reported row-level p = 0.0227","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":13,"end_line":20,"quoted_text":"| C01 | 3 | 3 |\n| C02 | 3 | 3 |\n| C03 | 3 | 3 |\n| C04 | 3 | 3 |\n| C05 | 3 | 3 |\n| C06 | 2 | 3 |\n| C07 | 1 | 3 |\n| C08 | 0 | 3 |"}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description itself states 'One trial is: one row', and the workflow follows that trial definition exactly; this could be read as authorizing the per-bout test. However, the same document designates colony_id as the independent-unit column and declares rows sharing a colony_id to be related, and a trial definition does not confer the independence the binomial procedure requires, so this does not overturn the finding.","observed_value":"trial defined as one row, but independence explicitly denied for rows sharing colony_id","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":12,"end_line":12,"quoted_text":"One trial is: one row"}]},{"description":"The report is transparent about its assumption and discloses the full per-colony breakdown, so nothing is hidden; but disclosure does not repair the test, and the disclosed breakdown itself evidences the within-colony dependence that invalidates the 24-trial assumption.","observed_value":"assumption disclosed; per-colony table provided","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":11,"end_line":12,"quoted_text":"| colony | UV picks | bouts |\n| --- | --- | --- |"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":25,"end_line":26,"quoted_text":"UV-pick probability of 0.500; each bout enters the test as one\nindependent trial."}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I tried to show the row-level test is harmless by re-running the analysis at the authorized independent unit. First I verified the reported statistic is internally correct: with 18 successes in 24 trials at p0 = 0.5, the exact two-sided p is 2 x 190051/2^24 ≈ 0.0227, matching the report, so the discrepancy is not a computation error. Then I aggregated to one outcome per colony: colonies C01-C06 are UV-majority (C06 at 2/3) while C07 and C08 are white-majority, giving 6 of 8 UV-majority colonies and an exact two-sided binomial p = 2 x (28+8+1)/256 ≈ 0.289 > 0.05; pooling raw visit counts within colony gives the same 6-of-8 split. I also checked whether the picks could plausibly be independent despite the shared colony label: the per-colony distribution (five colonies at 3/3, one at 0/3) is strongly overdispersed relative to independent Bernoulli(0.75) trials, confirming within-colony correlation. Every attempt to rescue the reported rejection at the colony level failed, so I could not falsify the issue.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":38061,"ttft_stream_ms":1688,"time_to_request_ms":13,"type":"result","duration_ms":77340,"uuid":"c6a61c3d-79cd-44b1-87f2-4ebca54c2bc2"}
